    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the offense, boasting a team-high 81.88 score against Painter. His massive 16% park and SP-skill boosts create the ideal conditions for a high-output performance, despite a marginal 1% drag from the opposing catcher\u2019s elite pop time. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** follows as our second-strongest option at 73.23; he is primed for a productive day thanks to an excellent 14% dynamic platoon advantage against Elder. Similarly, **Sam Antonacci** leverages a favorable matchup against Martinez to crack the top tier with a 65.85 score, primarily due to his leadoff role and the exploitable 4.84 xERA of the opposing starter.\n\nWhile the lineup is optimized for efficiency, the decision to bench **Jorge Polanco** (50.55) was the most difficult. He was narrowly excluded as his lower batting order position and negative park adjustment could not overcome the higher floors offered by our current UTIL and outfield starters. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Kyle Tucker**, whose 53.04 score is tempered by a daunting matchup against Suarez. While his base projection remains high, the SP skill penalty and lower lineup positioning cap his ceiling today. We remain cautious with **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jackson Merrill**, both of whom are facing negative platoon splits or difficult park factors that suppress their upside. We are continuing to monitor the status of **Jordan Westburg**, who remains sidelined on the IL, while keeping our depth pieces like **Heliot Ramos** and **Denzer Guzman** ready should mid-game adjustments prove necessary.",
